Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:44:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: drive letters without a mount manager (Wine patch 0913)

GetLogicalDrives took its letters from the mount manager, which runs in
a service the console never starts, so games saw no drives at all. A
game that looks up the drive it runs from found none and crashed. When
no drive is named, the drives are now the letters whose root folder
exists: the prefix's C: and Z:.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W9bbTPMqftZ2Yv6sJzUsWv
